# Reviewed upstream findings in the pinned runtime images (image-scan job only).
#
# Reviewed 2026-11-10 in Run 1.4. None of these can be fixed in this repository:
# each is in a package or binary shipped inside an upstream image, and the fix
# arrives only when upstream publishes a new image. They are listed one by one,
# so any NEW finding still fails the scan.
#
# Re-reviewed 2026-11-14 in Run 4.10. A scan with this file emptied still finds
# every entry on the pinned images. The newer upstream builds, postgres 18.7 and
# node 24.22.3-alpine (both 2026-11-12), carry the same findings. OpenBao 2.7.2
# and restic 0.19.1 are the latest releases. No pin moved.
#
# Every entry expires on 2026-12-14 (at most 30 days). After that date the scan
# fails again until each entry is re-reviewed or the image pin is moved to a
# fixed build.
#
# This file is never used for the repository's own dependencies (.trivyignore).

# postgres 18.6 — debian packages
# Debian has published the fix; the official postgres image has not been rebuilt with it yet.
# zlib1g 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+b1
CVE-2026-76844 exp:2026-12-14 # HIGH
CVE-2026-85091 exp:2026-12-14 # HIGH

# postgres 18.6 — debian krb5 libraries (libgssapi-krb5-2, libk5crypto3, libkrb5-3, libkrb5support0 1.21.3-5+deb13u1)
# Reviewed 2026-11-23 in Run 10.5: new upstream findings (the scan turned red overnight).
# Debian has the fix (1.21.3-5+deb13u2); the official postgres image has not been rebuilt with it.
# Exposed: nothing reachable. PostgreSQL loads the GSSAPI library, but no pg_hba line on any host
# or in dev uses gss, sspi or hostgssenc (only scram-sha-256 and reject), so no Kerberos exchange
# happens. Most entries are in the KDC and kadmind, which the image does not ship or run.
# Moving the pin is a runtime image change after Gate R (D-69): an owner question, not done here.
CVE-2026-107364 exp:2026-12-14 # HIGH
